<h1>How it compares</h1>

<p class="lede">I ran a homelab from a Mac and bought the alternatives
first. Each one ended the same way: a terminal open beside it, because no
window would show what was about to run, or where. If you already live in
yazi, ranger, or mc, pālana is that shape—two panes, vim keys, a preview, a
shell underneath—as a native Mac app that knows your hosts, the routes
between them, and their pools. The chart keeps the cells the others win.</p>

